data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":850,"item_id":"msg_06a57aab9881a9cd016b054debd47c87d18717907765b0f0f1","output_index":0,"content_index":0,"text":"{\"queries\":[],\"result_json\":\"{\\\"reviews\\\":[{\\\"actor\\\":\\\"sol\\\",\\\"decision\\\":\\\"reuse\\\",\\\"ability\\\":\\\"probe\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The existing general probe operation directly supports the feasible non-ingestive examination requested: observe a nearby source or accessible sample and report only measured findings. Its observe mode requires neither collection nor equipment. No supported examination here establishes edibility, toxin absence or nutritional composition. Related food trials, gathering and consultation add no necessary assessment mechanism; a new food-specific interface would duplicate probe.\\\",\\\"specification\\\":\\\"Reuse probe (equivalence open-baseline:probe:1, handler open.probe, revision foundation-open@1). Supply target as a currently visible, nearby subject reference, mode='observe', intensity=0; for example forest-plum-2 or start-2-nuts, provided the actor is actually within observation reach. The same operation applies to other accessible sources and samples, not just these instances. Revalidate visibility, reach and target existence at execution; remembered locations alone are insufficient. If necessary, the actor must separately navigate using actual travel time and energy. One completed observation takes one simulation round and 0.2 energy, with no material, reagent, tool, fuel or food cost. There are no prerequisites in the contract, but the actor must individually possess or learn the ability before execution; public registration does not grant mastery. No gathering is necessary for this version. Do not invoke press, wet or heat as part of observation, and do not assume water, heat, equipment or owned samples. Record only externally observable features actually supported by the handler, with target, time, method and evidence-event reference. Existing visible stock/stage information may be reobserved, but labels such as plum or hazelnut and a mature appearance do not establish species identification, edibility or safety. If no additional observable feature is supported, explicitly report that limitation rather than inventing an analysis. Keep visible-state observations distinct from unresolved toxicity, allergens, contamination, internal decay, digestibility and nutrient content; never expose hidden resource fields. Retain the unverified status of personal observations unless an existing verification rule independently warrants a stronger status. The operation neither consumes nor creates material: source stock and owned stacks, including item-4-sol-17 and item-27-sol-127, remain unchanged. It gives no nutrition, healing, detoxification or safety certification. Execution is one atomic interaction, not a persistent experiment. Interruption or cancellation before completion follows probe's cancel rule, yields no completed finding and retains no resumable work; a later attempt is a new paid interaction. Death likewise prevents completion. No spent time or energy is refunded, and no unperformed interaction may be charged as completed. There is no material reservation or material refund. Existing ambient growth and inventory decay continue normally during actual elapsed rounds; no new ongoing process, maintenance burden or physical product is introduced. Review and implementation waiting advance no simulation time. Enforce these established constraints in the existing execution code, not recurring model review.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":0,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"Requesting, consulting, registration and learning yield no experience benefit. A completed observation may qualify only through the existing evidence-deduplicated probe feedback for personally applicable, verified information gain, including a genuinely informative negative finding; an unsupported assay or generic statement of ignorance is not new evidence. Repeating the same visible finding cannot multiply rewards. Use existing bounded amounts, caps, cooldowns and decay; if no applicable coded rule establishes eligibility and magnitude, award zero rather than inventing one. No automatic pleasure, maintained satisfaction, comfort or nutrition benefit is attached to this reuse. Do not alter protected reward accounts, budgets, goals or permissions.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Reuse the existing probe observation event and visual metadata where supported. Each real attempt must distinguish completion, interruption and failure and reference the actual actor, target, method and tick. Any renderer should reuse target appearance and a generic observation indicator, not add a food-certification badge or reveal internal properties. Findings must identify their evidence event; incomplete or out-of-reach attempts must not display a completed observation. This review grants no new visual interface, success animation, inventory item or physical transformation.\\\"}]}\"}","logprobs":[]}

